.TH DB-PROBE 1 "2026-10-14" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
db-probe \- read-only SQL connectivity and server identity probe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B db-probe
.B --engine
.I postgresql|mysql|mariadb
.RI [ --host\ HOST ]
.RI [ --port\ N ]
.RI [ --user\ NAME ]
.RI [ --database\ NAME ]
.RI [ --timeout\ N ]
.RI [ --client\ ABSOLUTE_PATH ]
.RI [ --defaults-file\ ABSOLUTE_PATH ]
.RI [ --null ]
.br
.B db-probe --help | --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Executes one fixed read-only SQL identity/version query through a trusted
native psql, mysql or mariadb command-line client. Reports ENGINE, DATABASE,
DB_USER and VERSION. A successful TCP connection without valid SQL results
is not considered successful. Oracle and SQL Server are not yet supported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --engine
Required; postgresql, mysql or mariadb.
.TP
.B --host
Remote TCP host; without this, MySQL/MariaDB use a local Unix socket.
.TP
.B --port
TCP port 1 to 65535; requires --host.
.TP
.B --user, --database
Optional native-client login and database selection parameters.
.TP
.B --timeout
Client connection timeout, 1 to 30 seconds, default 5; total run timeout
is five seconds longer.
.TP
.B --client
Explicit absolute path to an executable trusted native client.
.TP
.B --defaults-file
MySQL/MariaDB only: private non-symlink client config file (mode 0600).
Only supported [client] credential and TLS options are allowed.
.TP
.B --null
Print the four fields as NUL-terminated strings, without headings.
.SH SECURITY
Passwords are never accepted as command-line options. PostgreSQL uses native
libpq authentication and forces TLS verify-full for TCP. MySQL forces TLS
VERIFY_IDENTITY, MariaDB enables certificate verification for TCP. No
user-supplied SQL or shell evaluation. Client stderr is suppressed to avoid
leaking secrets; invalid output or backend timeouts cause nonzero exit.
Uses bounded output and process runtime. Prefer read-only SQL accounts.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 valid SQL identity record; 1 connection/authentication/SQL failure;
2 invalid parameters; 3 missing native client, unsafe configuration, timeout
or unusable client output.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR psql (1),
.BR mysql (1),
.BR mariadb (1)
